  details:
    style: Five-name titulary
    first-monarch:
      - Narmer or Menes (as King of Upper and Lower Egypt)
      - Akhenaten or Thutmose III (first to be called Pharaoh)
    last-monarch:
      - Nectanebo II (last native)
      - Cleopatra and Caesarion (last Hellenistic pharaohs)
      - Maximinus Daza (last to have Egyptian royal titulary)
    formation:
      - c. 3150 BCE (first by tradition)
      - c. 1458 BCE or c. 1352 BCE (first to be called a pharaoh)
    abolition:
      - 343 BC (last native pharaoh)
      - 30 BC (last Hellenistic pharaohs)
      - 313 AD (last known use of ancient Egyptian royal titulary)
    residence: Varies by era
    appointer: Hereditary
